## 5. row invariance of design 2: each row alone vs inside the 16-row batch (the same fixed-order code)
  rows 0 / 7 / 15 alone == the batch's rows, all outputs bitwise: True

## 6. 'merge the two reads': (hn + inject (x) o) @ W^T = hn @ W^T + sum_s inject_s (o @ W_s^T) in fp64
  max |lhs - rhs| / max |lhs| = 7.4e-15: the identity holds, and the right side needs every one of the 4 weight slices (all 6.6 MB) plus the new rms; nothing is saved

(0.6 s, numpy 2.5.4, CPU only)
